<title>UK: UK tax rates should be lower, Clarke says.</title>
<headline>UK tax rates should be lower, Clarke says.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-10-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>UK tax rates should be lower but the government will not borrow to finance tax cuts, UK Chancellor of the Exchequer Kenneth Clarke said in an interview with the Evening Standard newspaper.  </p>
<p>&quot;That the tax level should be lower I am in no doubt. But I am not going to borrow the money to do it,&quot; he said in the interview.</p>
</text>
